+## 24. Continuous transparency enforcement (additive, 2026-11-24)
+
+`docs/CONTINUOUS-ENFORCEMENT.md` is the normative rule that the transparency
+policy cannot regress silently. It is not a claim that transparency was
+achieved; it is the rule that a transparency claim cannot outrun its evidence.
+
+**The enforcement points are named, and each refuses.** The rule is enforced by
+`forensics/tools/release_gate.py` item 10 (`check_transparency`), which calls
+`forensics/tools/continuous_enforcement.py` and maps each refusal to one gate
+row. The codes are `CE_REFUSED_PROFILE_ABSENT`, `CE_REFUSED_REGISTRY_STALE`,
+`CE_REFUSED_PUBLICATION_CLAIM`, `CE_REFUSED_PROFILE_NOT_ADMITTED`,
+`CE_REFUSED_SCHEMA_FIELD_ABSENT`, `CE_REFUSED_UNBOUND_CLAIM`,
+`CE_REFUSED_NONCLAIMS_ABSENT` and `CE_REFUSED_ENFORCEMENT_REGRESSION`. Every one
+has a control in `evidence/b8/CONTROLS.json` and a test in
+`forensics/tools/tests/test_continuous_enforcement.py`.
+
+**The claim schema carries a closed field.** `evidence/etp/claim.schema.json`
+defines an optional `transparency` object with a closed state enum
+(`NOT_ADMITTED`, `ADMITTED`, `PUBLISHED`), a closed profile enum, two SHA-256
+digests and an RFC 3339 timestamp. There is no free text. A claim whose
+`authority.kind` is `public-transparency-log` must carry the field. No committed
+claim carries it today, so the absence check is vacuous: record that, do not
+report it as coverage.
+
+**The public non-claims are mandatory.** `docs/TRANSPARENCY-NON-CLAIMS.md`
+states, with the record that shows each, that there is no admitted Rekor
+service, no witness, no trusted timestamp, no publication and no independent
+reproduction. The requirement is §B.29's SEAL and EXTERNAL rows. Deleting a row
+is a refused release, not a documentation edit.
+
+**The enforcement itself is checked.** A gate item that disappears, item 10
+losing its wiring, the enforcement record or the normative document going
+missing, or a previously checked refusal code no longer being named is
+`CE_REFUSED_ENFORCEMENT_REGRESSION`. The rule is a tripwire for the ordinary
+single-edit regression, not tamper-proofing against a coordinated removal.
+
+**Two applications are pending, not done.** `forensics/etp8/agents-patch.diff`
+(this section) is `PENDING_MAINTAINER_APPLICATION` because this file is the
+user's standing document. `forensics/etp8/ci-transparency-job.patch` is
+`PENDING_CREDENTIAL` because the pushing credential lacks the `workflow` scope.
+Until they are applied, item 10 runs in the release gate and the tools suite,
+not on every push.
+
+**What it does not establish.** A passing item 10 does not establish
+publication, admission, witnessing, timestamping, archival or independent
+reproduction, and does not show that the profile conforms to any external
+standard. Those are `NOT_RUN` in `docs/CONTINUOUS-ENFORCEMENT.md` §9.
